# Test Conventions

## File Naming
- Unit tests: `tests/<subdir>/test_<module>.py`
- Integration tests: `tests/<subdir>/test_integration_<scope>.py`
- Workflow tests: `tests/test_<name>_workflow.py`
- Stability/chaos tests: `tests/test_stability_<scenario>.py`

## Markers
Use module-level `pytestmark = pytest.mark.<marker>` to tag entire files.

| Marker | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `integration` | Requires external services (excluded by default) |
| `distributed` | Multi-worker Ray pipelines |
| `workflow` | End-to-end pipeline tests |
| `slow` | Takes >30s |
| `chaos` | Random failure injection (not in CI) |
| `benchmark` | Performance benchmarks (excluded by default) |

## Fixtures (conftest.py)
- `ray_cluster` — function-scoped Ray local cluster, no GPUs
- `ray_cluster_with_gpus` — function-scoped, 16 fake GPUs (for serve tests)

## Commands
```bash
cd engine
uv run pytest tests/ -v --tb=short -m "not integration"   # unit
uv run pytest tests/ -v --tb=short -m "integration"        # integration
```

## WorkQueue in Tests
Use `workqueue_db_path="memory://"` for in-memory queue (no persistence).
